  "problem": "$\\int \\frac{2}{|y|\\sqrt{{y}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}y=$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|y|\\sqrt{{y}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}y=\\text{arcsec}\\,y.\n$$\n\nThen we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{|y|\\sqrt{{y}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|y|\\sqrt{{y}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\text{\u00a0arcsec\u00a0}y+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
